<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72186" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰᾱκ-ίζω</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰηκ-</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>steer</i>: hence, <i>govern, guide, manage,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τελαμῶσι σκυτίνοις οἰηκίζοντες [τὰς
					ἀσπίδας]</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.171
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ἵππους] οἰ.</span>
			<i>guide</i> them (when swimming), <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.43.4
			</span></i>, etc. :—
				Pass.
			, of horses, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ ῥαβδίου -ίζεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					17.3.7
				</span></i>
			 ; of the seasons, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				9.914
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ πάντα οἰ. Κεραυνός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Heraclit.
					64
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς νέους -οντες ἡδονῇ καὶ λύπῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1172a21
				</span></i>
			 :—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ κοινὸς βίος ὥσπερ ὑπὸ θεῶν τινος
					-όμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					18.59
				</span></i>
			.</div>
